-- §3 determination, #3437's Array Float face.  Drained must-fail pin
-- `3437-indexed-literal-compare-defaults-to-int`, kept here as the regression
-- guard ([G-PIN-DRAIN]).  `a[0] == 1` poses `Index (Array Float) ?k ?v` with
-- `Num ?k`, `Num ?v` and `Eq ?v`.  `Index (Array a) Int a` is the one instance
-- that unifies, and it is consistent with the siblings (`Float` has `Num` and
-- `Eq`), so `?k = Int` and `?v = Float` before either literal defaults; `1`
-- is the Float 1.0.  Defaulting first rejected it with "Type mismatch: Int vs
-- Float".
-- Hand-derived: element 0 of [|1.0|] is 1.0, so True on all three verbs.
f : Array Float -> Bool
f a = a[0] == 1

main = println (f [|1.0|])
